      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, here is a quick checklist for your fintech app's accessibility audit regarding WCAG 2.1 color contrast and screen reader compatibility.\n\n**Color Contrast:**\n*   **1.4.3 Contrast (Minimum):** Ensure all text has a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1 against its background.\n*   **1.4.3 Contrast (Enhanced):** For large text (18pt+ or 14pt+ bold), ensure a contrast ratio of at least 3:1.\n*   **1.4.11 Non-text Contrast:** Check that non-text graphical objects (like icons or charts) have a contrast ratio of at least 3:1.\n*   **1.4.12 Text Spacing:** Avoid text that is too small or lacks spacing to ensure readability.\n\n**Screen Reader Compatibility:**\n*   **1.3.1 Info and Relationships:** Ensure all content is presented in a way that allows screen readers to convey the relationships between elements (e.g., using proper heading levels).\n*   **1.3.2 Meaningful Sequence:** Verify that the reading order of the content makes logical sense to the user.\n*",
